SM(299,{"n":"Exodus 20.7-17","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Exodus 20.7-17.mp3","d":2492.8,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.92,"Verse 7. You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain, for the Lord will not hold him guiltless who takes his name in vain."],[32.88,"Okay. So a number of these, there's a way we're used to reading this, and it's usually wrong."],[40.74,"Or at least incomplete."],[43.06,"Or a little weak."],[45.43,"Um, so what this meant when I grew up, basically, was that you weren't allowed to say uh God or a certain selection of other words directly related to God as an expletive."],[67.87,"There were a whole bunch of other expletives that were okay because they weren't overtly religious."],[73.03,"Like number one."],[74.39,"And number two, you could say sort of versions of it like gosh darn it."],[82.39,"See, it's better because I changed a couple of letters."],[87.32,"Um I hate to tell you that's not what this is about."],[98.92,"That's not that's not what this is about."],[101.32,"Uh I'm not afraid to be controversial, so I'll do it again"],[106.56,"Uh the issue with expletives is not the words."],[112.26,"We have this idea there's bad words."],[114.5,"And everybody interestingly, everybody's list of bad words is a little different, usually based on the family they grew up in."],[121.38,"There's some things that are bad words for other families that weren't in theirs, and vice versa."],[127.86,"So let me tell you, there are no bad words."],[130.9,"Even the one you're thinking of right now when I said that."],[135.56,"There are no bad words."],[137.16,"There are only bad intentions."],[141.6,"Okay? You can deeply hurt and destroy someone. with your words without ever saying one of those bad words"],[150.88,"And the fact that you didn't say one of those bad words doesn't make it better."],[160.45,"And if you smash your thumb with a hammer, this is the one that's gonna get people mad at me."],[166.45,"If you smash your thumb with a hammer, really doesn't matter if you just howl in pain or you let out one of the bad words."],[174.77,"You smashed your thumb with a hammer."],[178.69,"It hurts. Okay?"],[182.49,"And if you're telling dirty jokes, it doesn't matter if you use the cuss words or if you use substitute words, you're still telling dirty jokes."],[188.57,"Like you're not tricking God"],[193.71,"By using like medical terminology or something."],[199.95,"Okay? Let's be adults."],[203.84,"Okay. So what is this about?"],[207.38,"What is this about?"],[209.38,"Okay. You do not take the name Yahweh in vain."],[212.66,"Pharisees found a cool way around this."],[215.06,"We'll never say it, we'll never write it, and that way we can't take it in vain."],[219.3,"Or so they thought."],[221.7,"Again, not the point."],[225.7,"Missing the point."],[227.06,"Now I'm not saying you should go around yelling it."],[229.06,"ing it Or us in expletives."],[230.18,"I'm not saying that's a positive thing"],[230.42,"Right. But what this is about is God says over and over again that there are people and places where he's placing his name."],[251.43,"One of those peoples is the people of Israel."],[255.51,"He is identifying himself."],[257.83,"Yahweh, the God of Israel."],[262.65,"So they're receiving the name Yahweh."],[265.53,"What does that mean?"],[266.97,"That means people are going to look at those people, how they live, how they act, what they do."],[276.45,"And that's going to reflect on what they think of Yahweh, what they think of Israel's God."],[288.02,"And so if they do that, and then behave badly, behave in horrible ways, that's going to bring dishonor to the name of Yahweh."],[302.18,"That's what this is talking about."],[305.1,"Okay? That's certainly happening today, where many people who are anti-Christian say they are anti-Christian because of the behavior of Christians."],[314.63,"And rightly so in some cases."],[317.03,"Rightly so. If you are going to call yourself a Christian, you are taking the name of Christ, putting it on yourself."],[327.93,"And people are going to think things about Christ, about Christianity, about God, based on what you do and how you act."],[338.33,"And so this commandment is about this is a serious thing."],[344.73,"I have a funny version of breaking this as commandment, which is the guy who has the honk if you love Jesus bumper sticker, and you honk Adam and he flips you the bird."],[356.86,"But if we really took this seriously, there are a lot of people out there wearing Jesus t-shirts."],[366.3,"That act in certain ways."],[370.27,"When I was a kid, it was everybody had the fish on their car."],[374.85,"Or you might have an orthodox sticker or bumper sticker on your car."],[377.75,"When you identify yourself with Christ publicly in front of people, that conveys this great responsibility."],[388.01,"To bring honor to his name."],[393.21,"Okay? And we're gonna get into this is the same kind of dynamic behind the honor your father and mother."],[400.33,"Frankly, that we're gonna get to here in a minute."],[403.21,"But that's what this is talking about."],[403.53,"'s what this is talking about That."],[404.65,"That we're called to something higher"],[411.88,"When we take the name of God and put it on ourselves."],[420.6,"Verse 8 Remember the Sabbath day to keep it holy."],[423.96,"Six days you shall labor and do all your work, but the seventh day is the Sabbath of the Lord your God."],[429.4,"In it you shall do no work, neither you nor your son, nor your daughter, your male servant, your female servant, your cattle, nor your stranger who sojourns with you."],[439.4,"For in six days the Lord made heaven and earth, the sea and everything in them, and rested on the seventh day."],[444.68,"Therefore the Lord blessed the Sabbath day and hallowed it."],[450.32,"So they're not to do anything on the seventh day."],[454.8,"Now we talked back in Genesis about how God rested on it doesn't mean he took a break."],[459.7,"That rested there is talking about him sitting enthroned."],[462.66,"And so he blessed that day."],[465.94,"Now we tend to, from our modern perspective and our modern view of labor, we say, oh, that's a day of rest, because like you're tired, you're worn out after the week."],[475.14,"You know, we usually want two days off."],[477.3,"But oh, you get a day off."],[480.9,"God's doing something nice for you."],[483.04,"And giving you this day off."],[486.0,"But we have to remember who this is originally given to, and most of the history of the world, where most people are farming."],[495.8,"And there's as we go forward, there's not only going to be Sabbath days, there's going to be Sabbath years."],[501.4,"They're supposed to follow."],[503.96,"So your crop yield."],[508.18,"Whether you have a good harvest or a bad harvest, how well you've sown your seed, how well you've irrigated, all these things."],[515.62,"For these folks who are subsistence farming, this is you know whether all your children will survive the winter."],[525.31,"This isn't just about paying bills and getting, you know, a Netflix subscription."],[529.87,"This is will your whole family live?"],[533.73,"Will you live?"],[535.41,"Will you have to sell some of your kids into slavery, literally, to survive?"],[540.41,"Will you have to sell yourself into slavery to survive?"],[546.17,"And so God says, one day out of seven, you're taking a break."],[549.29,"You're not doing anything."],[551.69,"And notice how he breaks it down."],[553.61,"Oh, by the way, when I say you're not doing anything, I mean you're not doing anything."],[558.57,"You're not sending your slaves out there to work for you."],[563.13,"You're not sending your kids out to work."],[564.97,"You're not putting your animals to work."],[569.21,"No. You're not sending the foreigner out to work for you."],[575.29,"You're taking a break."],[576.97,"A little later, he's gonna say, every seventh year, you're taking a break for a year."],[581.29,"You're gonna leave the field"],[586.93,"You're gonna let the uh the poor go out there and get what they need out of it."],[594.05,"But you're not gonna touch it, you're not gonna harvest it."],[596.37,"So, what does this require?"],[597.57,"This isn't a break."],[599.94,"This is this is God requiring a great deal of trust from them."],[607.91,"They've got to trust God."],[610.23,"That if they're doing what God told them to do, that he'll take care of them."],[614.87,"That he'll take care of the crops, that he'll take care of the yield."],[619.83,"But that's also teaching them something."],[623.23,"And it's not actually them that's making the crops grow."],[628.83,"They can't get it to rain the right amount."],[633.07,"They can't get the seed to be good seed."],[635.23,"They can't stop blight."],[636.43,"They can't stop locusts and other bugs."],[641.63,"They can deceive themselves into thinking, oh no, this is all based on my hard work."],[649.15,"But the reality is it's God who's providing for them."],[653.23,"And by making them take these breaks and trust him, it's reinforcing that to them."],[661.39,"Trying to help them understand."],[663.55,"Trying to help them trust."],[666.27,"And this isn't just, oh, God demands that you trust him."],[669.39,"This is better for them"],[672.5,"This is what Christ is getting at when he talks to a bunch of dirt poor peasants."],[676.5,"I mean, poverty beyond what we can imagine as poverty, the people Jesus was talking to in Galilee."],[683.06,"And tells them, don't worry about what you're gonna eat and what you're gonna drink and what you're gonna wear."],[688.82,"And most of them are probably sitting there thinking, all I do is worry about what I'm gonna eat and what I'm gonna drink and what I'm gonna wear and my kids and my things."],[696.8,"That's all I think about."],[699.54,"He says, don't think about that."],[701.14,"Why? Because God is the one who's taking care of you."],[707.25,"When they come to the point of trust and admit that it's not based on them and their hard work."],[711.17,"It's God It's not them doing it."],[714.09,"They can. If they really trust God."],[721.54,"They go ahead and say, I just need to be doing what God wants me to do."],[725.38,"I need to be being faithful to God, and then God's going to take care of the rest of this."],[729.3,"And I don't have to worry all the time."],[732.66,"I don't have to be up all night."],[735.62,"I don't have to, you know, toil."],[739.4,"So ultimately it is a gift."],[741.66,"Teaching them to trust God is a gift if they're willing to learn it."],[745.68,"And I think it's obvious how this applies to us too."],[750.0,"Because we're maybe even more likely if we're getting a paycheck from somewhere."],[754.0,"Look here's how many hours I work."],[754.08,"right This is my."],[754.2,"Who made you healthy enough to do it"],[754.22,"Well, this is my hard work."],[761.98,"Who kept you alive to do it?"],[767.83,"On and on and on."],[769.13,"It's God who's providing it."],[770.73,"But again, if we learn that."],[775.62,"It's not just up to me."],[777.14,"My survival is not just up to me in this world."],[780.18,"God can't take a year off."],[782.9,"Well, he's not asking you to take a year off."],[784.9,"Yeah Oh, 2020, he kind of made us all take a year."],[789.7,"That was a whole other story."],[794.9,"Verse 12 Honor your father and mother. that it may be well with you, and your days may be long upon the good land the Lord your God is giving you"],[806.3,"So this is one that again, surprise, surprise, uh, we misinterpret."],[811.18,"Part of this is because parents want us to misinterpret."],[814.22,"Parents want us to think this means obey your father and your mother."],[818.38,"Do whatever your father and mother tell you."],[822.67,"And I don't blame parents for doing that."],[824.69,"Any port in a storm, anything you could do, the struggle is real."],[827.98,"I get it."],[829.1,"But right, but that's not what it means."],[832.86,"That's not what it means."],[834.62,"Sort of like what we were talking about in uh the taking the name of the Lord in vain."],[839.66,"What this commandment is saying is that. that you need to live your life in a way brings honor to your father and your mother"],[846.82,"In our modern terms, your family name."],[854.26,"So that you're living a life where people look at you, and whether it's true or not, say, wow, you must have come from a great family."],[863.94,"Because if they see you and how you live your life."],[885.06,"Any more than we could. get there by always 100% doing what we want to do"],[892.54,"But we can live in our life in a way that brings honor and not dishonor."],[897.24,"And not disrespect."],[899.82,"To in our modern terms, our family name, to our parents, to our family, to our heritage."],[906.11,"We can do that."],[911.79,"Some of these are a little clearer."],[914.83,"You shall not murder."],[920.89,"We will expand on this a little bit because there are questions that come into this, because of course, define murder."],[929.3,"Um that's because of course there's other instances of killing."],[934.18,"I'll be blunt."],[935.14,"What this means, I mean we saw this back in Genesis 9 after the flood with Noah."],[940.63,"Taking a human life is always wrong."],[942.79,"It is never good."],[945.35,"Never. It's never good."],[947.67,"Even if we want to say justified, that doesn't, it's not even neutral."],[952.39,"It's always bad."],[955.43,"It's always bad."],[958.15,"When I talk about this, there's always somebody."],[960.87,"I'm not saying there's someone in this room, but there's someone out there who will say, oh, well, what about, you know, if you're fighting in a war?"],[969.01,"Talk to someone who's killed someone in a war."],[971.25,"They will tell you it was not good"],[976.63,"They will tell you, they'll tell you it's what they had to do, maybe."],[981.25,"In the circumstance."],[982.53,"Or what about self defense?"],[984.13,"Talk to someone who's had to kill someone in self-defense."],[989.97,"Ask them how they actually feel about it."],[993.01,"Whether they think it was good."],[995.01,"They're gonna tell you that it's not."],[999.09,"I'll take this even further."],[1000.85,"Talk to someone who's been in a car accident where someone died."],[1005.01,"And the car accident wasn't even their fault, and ask them how they feel about it."],[1011.18,"They're not gonna be like, well, it was accident wasn't my fault, so it's cool."],[1015.7,"That's not real."],[1016.98,"That's not real life."],[1019.32,"Real life is every human is made in the image of God, as Genesis 9 reminds us."],[1025.82,"And so any time a human life is taken, at any stage of fetal development, at any stage of old age."],[1036.52,"Anytime a human life is taken, that is a tragedy."],[1039.72,"That is a horrible thing."],[1043.85,"Even when, due to the sinful world we live in, it may have been the best bad option in that moment."],[1054.17,"It's still a horrible thing."],[1058.21,"And that's why any form of taking another human life, the church has always penanced."],[1065.47,"Not punished, penanced, meaning the church has always established a process by which someone who has done that, longer or shorter, depending on the circumstances."],[1079.81,"Adapted to the circumstances of the particular situation, but established a process by which a person who's had to do that gets reintegrated into the community."],[1092.21,"And can experience healing from what's happened."],[1096.55,"And restoration. When I say the church has always done that, I'm talking about all the way, we're going to see that in the Torah as we go forward."],[1105.15,"God will say to the Israelites, you need to go and wipe out this giant clan."],[1111.07,"And Israel goes and does it."],[1114.43,"And then all the soldiers are going to be unclean."],[1118.27,"And they're going to go through a process of washing their weapons, washing their armor, living outside the camp."],[1125.36,"You say, well, they're just doing what God just told them to do."],[1128.56,"God told them to do it because it had to be done, because of the evil things that group was doing."],[1133.76,"They had to put a stop to it."],[1135.04,"But that still doesn't make killing them good."],[1138.41,"Now they need to go through this process."],[1140.81,"So what we call PTSD or whatever we call it."],[1143.53,"And the church has always known about it"],[1144.34,"God knew about that already."],[1146.76,"It's in the Torah."],[1150.28,"And it set up this process of spiritual healing and restoration for those people who have gone through that."],[1156.84,"That's not a punishment."],[1159.72,"That's how healing gets worked out."],[1161.8,"Just telling those people, oh no, it's fine, it's fine."],[1164.28,"It was justified in the circumstances."],[1166.2,"That doesn't help them."],[1173.16,"We're in the home stretch."],[1176.12,"You shall not commit adultery."],[1179.72,"That one should be clear."],[1181.4,"There was an old SNL sketch."],[1183.96,"You'll know how old it is as soon as I tell you about it, where uh Moses is uh it was John Goodman playing Moses."],[1190.08,"He's reading the Ten Commandments, and he gets to this one about adultery."],[1193.6,"And uh Bill Clinton steps out of the crowd and says, Well, uh, can you be more specific?"],[1198.8,"Um that's from the 90s."],[1202.48,"But anyway. Uh so adultery here, if you need to get more specific, Christ gets more specific."],[1212.08,"You look at a woman lustfully, that's adultery."],[1219.92,"So you don't even have to."],[1221.68,"It's not a question of, well, what if you just do this?"],[1223.76,"Or what if you just don't have to do anything."],[1227.65,"Don't have to do anything."],[1229.94,"Now, you notice. you said, look at a woman lustfully"],[1233.87,"This is an important point that we're gonna get to as we go through these commandments, especially commandments related to sexual issues."],[1240.27,"This is the first one, the one against adultery."],[1242.51,"You're gonna notice they're all directed toward men."],[1247.87,"This does not mean that women cannot commit sexual sins."],[1251.15,"Obviously, they can."],[1253.79,"But what this means was in the Bronze Age, women didn't get to make choices about those kinds of things."],[1260.35,"That's the reality of the world in the Bronze Age."],[1264.83,"If you were a woman when you were like 12 or 13, your family married you off to someone."],[1272.83,"And he would have sex with you whenever he felt like it."],[1278.41,"And if he decided he was tired of you, he would divorce you."],[1284.33,"And you'd go back to your family, and that was probably it for you."],[1288.65,"If your parents were gone, you'd probably end up being a prostitute because there wasn't another way to make a living."],[1293.85,"That's the reality of the Bronze Age."],[1298.86,"So there's no point in God giving commandments about sexuality to women in that context, where they can't make decisions and choices."],[1311.44,"Where they can't make decisions and choices."],[1313.68,"Men held all the power in terms of making those choices, so God gives all the commandments to men. to protect women from them for the most part"],[1322.76,"And other men and"],[1348.41,"It comes out of the early church, martyrs like St."],[1351.85,"Thecla. Where the early Christians said, no, women have a right to not get married."],[1362.5,"And to devote themselves to God."],[1366.82,"That's where it started."],[1369.8,"Christianity said women get at least that choice."],[1372.89,"At least that choice."],[1373.93,"They have the right to say no to marriage."],[1376.09,"But that was huge."],[1379.85,"Yeah. And St."],[1380.89,"Thecla got martyred for it."],[1383.53,"But once Christians got into power, then that right got enshrined."],[1388.17,"And that was the beginning of the idea."],[1390.71,"But now that women are free to make those choices, what that means is the commandments apply to them too."],[1398.36,"Just as much."],[1399.96,"Meaning, if a woman looks at a man with lust in her heart, she has committed adultery with him."],[1405.17,"The converse is now applicable."],[1408.05,"It's not that it ever wasn't, but realistically, in the culture we're talking about."],[1414.95,"So I say, very good thing that women now get to make choices about this."],[1420.39,"That also brings with it responsibility."],[1425.75,"In those regards."],[1428.47,"You shall not steal."],[1433.91,"Okay. So we're gonna have to do a brief thing here."],[1440.87,"Yeah, we can still do it."],[1442.15,"Okay, we're not too bad."],[1443.83,"Um you shall not seal."],[1446.91,"So uh we have a different view of property in the modern world than they did in the ancient world."],[1453.39,"There's a distinction that we mostly don't know about or think about now between private property and personal property."],[1460.43,"Okay, personal property existed in the ancient world."],[1463.63,"The concept of private property did not."],[1466.91,"Here's the distinction."],[1468.75,"Personal property is there are things that belong to me, I use them."],[1473.73,"To use a modern example, my toothbrush."],[1476.59,"My coffee mug, my cell phone."],[1479.31,"These are all examples of personal property."],[1481.15,"My reading glasses."],[1483.04,"These are things that are mine that I use."],[1485.68,"Personal property. That exists in the ancient world."],[1488.64,"Private property is the idea that I can, for example, delimit a piece of land and say, this is mine, no one else can go there."],[1501.12,"That didn't exist in the ancient world."],[1504.58,"This idea that I could section something off and say who can and can't go there."],[1509.38,"Or a house I don't live in."],[1513.76,"Say, that's mine, no one else can go there."],[1518.26,"I had a house, but it was the house I was living in, the house I was using."],[1521.16,"Like this personal property idea."],[1523.76,"Um why is this an important distinction to make?"],[1527.92,"Well, we're gonna see in Deuteronomy when we get into some of the more specific commandments."],[1533.64,"There's gonna be a commandment that says that if there's a famine and you don't have enough food to feed your family, and someone else has stockpiled food, they have more food than they need, you can go and take enough food to feed your family, and that's not stealing."],[1555.56,"If you take more than you need, you're stealing."],[1560.12,"But if you take what you need to feed your family, you're not stealing."],[1562.84,"In fact, him by stockpiling it when other people didn't have what they needed, he's stealing."],[1568.76,"Okay So, from the perspective of that those commandments in Deuteronomy, taking what we would now call private. property is not stealing"],[1580.37,"In fact, having what we would now call private property is stealing."],[1587.06,"Taking someone else's personal property is stealing."],[1593.94,"I come into your house."],[1596.39,"You come over here, punch me in the face, and take my cell phone."],[1599.65,"That's stealing. You don't have enough food to eat."],[1604.06,"I've got a stocked fridge with stuff rotting in it."],[1607.1,"You come into my house and just take a sandwich and leave without breaking anything."],[1613.02,"You're fine, according to the Torah."],[1616.38,"That's not stealing."],[1617.9,"Jean Valjean, totally cool."],[1620.06,"Accord according according to the Torah"],[1625.84,"But if we don't understand this, then so there's gonna be there's a whole bunch of quotes in the church fathers that we won't understand if we don't understand this principle."],[1634.08,"Like what St."],[1635.04,"Basil the Great says, all of the shoes in your closet belong to the poor and you're stealing them."],[1643.28,"And I post that on social media and get called a socialist."],[1647.7,"That's I'm a commie."],[1649.07,"If I post I' liked that, say basil the great."],[1652.07,"But that's based on this view."],[1655.09,"Yes, you have your shoes that you wear and you need to wear."],[1658.69,"But if you have a whole bunch of shoes, pairs of shos ofes. shoes, and there' a bunch people out there with no"],[1666.89,"That's part of the outrage of um the disparity."],[1673.61,"We call it the you know that wealth gap or corporations, or or you know, maybe there's something ingrained, you know, that's part of us that says, yeah, that's just not right."],[1685.13,"Yeah. And so that's here, yeah."],[1689.37,"Here in the Torah, that's part of God's right."],[1693.13,"If I want to have five pairs of shoes, fine, unless I've got a neighbor who has none."],[1699.29,"Now not fine."],[1701.13,"Now I need to give one of those pairs of shoes to him."],[1704.81,"Then things are fine."],[1706.95,"And that's what's behind what Christ says about if someone steals this from you, give them this too."],[1713.48,"It's the same idea."],[1714.52,"Like, well, obviously they need it."],[1719.02,"It's not like there was a big market for secondhand cloaks."],[1722.7,"You know, if they're stealing your cloak, it's because they need what they're cold."],[1726.76,"Like. That's stealing."],[1746.65,"You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor"],[1751.97,"Okay, this means don't lie."],[1754.9,"Wrong. Emmanuel Kant has entered the chat."],[1761.06,"Um literally, that's where we get the idea."],[1765.06,"Um, so you shall not bear false witness against your neighbor is very literal."],[1770.34,"Bearing false witness."],[1771.38,"This is talking about testifying."],[1774.91,"Now, specifically, it's talking about testifying."],[1777.71,"They didn't have courts."],[1778.69,"They went before the city gates."],[1780.71,"But you would have to have two witnesses who would make the same accusation against somebody."],[1786.23,"Then we put on trial."],[1787.19,"So this is talking about making false accusations."],[1791.03,"This is about condemning other people falsely"],[1791.39,"That's what this commandment is about."],[1796.51,"We could do that for all kinds of reasons."],[1798.97,"So this commandment is more against gossip than lying, for example."],[1806.19,"Certain forms of lying."],[1807.23,"Obviously, you lie under orthodox case."],[1809.39,"Yeah. This applies."],[1811.4,"But gossip is violating this commandment."],[1814.3,"Slandering someone is violating this commandment."],[1817.02,"Ruining someone's reputation is violating this commandment."],[1821.9,"That's what this commandment is really talking about."],[1826.0,"So Immanuel Kant did this whole thing with lying."],[1829.36,"It was his favorite example."],[1830.8,"Well, what if everyone lied?"],[1832.56,"Then the whole world would fall apart."],[1833.84,"So you have to always tell the truth"],[1836.58,"And so you get the people who are like, so as much as I hate using the Nazis as an example, but I have to in this case."],[1843.62,"Try to be more creative."],[1844.98,"I try to talk about the Khmer Rouge or something."],[1847.7,"But the uh, you know, Nazi soldiers come to your door."],[1851.78,"Are you hiding any Jews that you are?"],[1853.86,"You have to say yes, because lying is wrong."],[1858.5,"Of course you don't have to say yes."],[1864.79,"Of course you don't have to say yes."],[1870.12,"That's that's ridiculous."],[1871.4,"The problem is not, and we've already seen examples like in Genesis with Judah and Tamar."],[1875.8,"We've seen examples and with Jacob where people use deception."],[1880.32,"And that's the trick in the sense of deception and trickery, where your motive, it's like hiding something from a child, but in the sense of not telling and diverting."],[1895.6,"You don't change the truth, you just divert attention."],[1899.28,"You don't go up to a three-year-old and say everyone you know will be dead someday."],[1904.1,"Like, it's true."],[1906.9,"It's true, but you don't say that."],[1909.91,"Like, and you're not lying by not saying that."],[1914.01,"Like that. This idea is just ridiculous."],[1919.79,"Like that, but but yeah, in Genesis, it's particularly the idea is use deception to bring about justice, then it's not a sin."],[1929.2,"Because deception is often all you have."],[1932.16,"Like Tamar, who is a woman, you know, who is a widow twice over, who had been sent back to her family."],[1939.44,"She had no power."],[1940.08,"She could print court case."],[1941.68,"There's nothing she could do to get justice except use deception."],[1946.54,"Use deception to tell the Brio's right."],[1949.82,"And so, yeah, Nazi soldiers have a lot more power than Dutch families hiding Jewish people."],[1957.66,"The only way they could bring about justice, i.e. save an innocent life, is deception."],[1962.78,"That's not what this commandment is about"],[1968.8,"That's not what this commandment is about."],[1971.22,"And by the way, that's the way Jewish people have always interpreted this."],[1978.07,"For example, they will say, saving a human life, because of what we talked about when we were talking about murder."],[1984.61,"Saving a human life never violates a commandment."],[1989.73,"You can, on the surface, violate any commandment in the Torah in their interpretation in order to save a human life."],[1997.73,"So you break the Sabbath to save a human life."],[2002.03,"You you uh lie to save a human life."],[2005.81,"You you would potentially bear false witness in court to save a human life."],[2009.43,"To um, I don't know how committing adultery would save a human life, but whatever."],[2015.23,"Like you get the idea."],[2018.21,"You get the idea."],[2019.7,"So the whole Kant's categorical imperative."],[2023.46,"Well, imagine everyone lied."],[2025.06,"So, see, that would be bad."],[2026.42,"So we have to all tell the truth all it."],[2030.26,"18th century Germans, man."],[2032.02,"What are you gonna do?"],[2033.54,"Um. So again, this is about destroying the reputation of another person."],[2039.2,"Gossip. Slander. Going to court and testifying them, just accusing, making false accusations in general."],[2046.68,"These are things that are epidemic, in our society"],[2050.97,"There's whole magazines of TV channels made up purely of this."],[2056.97,"And people delighting in it."],[2063.29,"And finally, the final one or two commandments, depending on if you split them."],[2075.13,"And neither shall you covet his field, nor his male servant, his female servant, his ox, his donkey, any of his cattle, or whatever belongs to your neighbor."],[2087.93,"So sometimes you hear this thing."],[2090.29,"I bet you've heard it, where they'll say, Oh, see, when Christ talks about the commandments in the gospels, he like ratchets it up, he makes it more difficult."],[2103.19,"Because they just weren't supposed to commit adultery."],[2105.51,"But like we said earlier, he said, if you lust after a woman in your heart, you've already committed adultery."],[2110.23,"And they thought you just weren't supposed to murder people, but Jesus says, if you say to your brother, you fool."],[2115.77,"If you hate him, you've already killed him."],[2117.63,"How many of you have heard that?"],[2119.15,"Yeah. Okay. Uh this is why that's wrong."],[2124.19,"Because what is this?"],[2126.51,"Coveting your neighbor's wife is what?"],[2128.75,"Envying her? Or thinking about committing adultery."],[2133.55,"'s Coveting your neighbor personal property is what?"],[2134.58,"Thinking about stealing"],[2138.24,"Stealing. That's why this one's here."],[2146.55,"This is all the thinking and the planning and the fantasizing and the dwelling upon."],[2152.81,"That precedes those other commandments."],[2159.58,"The wanting, the desiring."],[2162.62,"So you talk yourself into oh no, I need it."],[2165.98,"Or this is the even this is the right thing to do."],[2168.7,"Yeah, it's all in there."],[2170.7,"But that's why this commandment is there."],[2172.94,"This is the lead in to all the others."],[2176.24,"This is the lead in to all the others."],[2178.0,"And this is an important step back."],[2181.62,"This is an important step back."],[2182.98,"Because the truth is, every sin we commit in terms of a sinful action starts out as a thought."],[2193.46,"It starts out as a thought that enters into our head."],[2205.22,"They fly through our head."],[2206.66,"We have a thousand of them a day."],[2208.82,"We have no real control over them."],[2212.76,"Part of the discipline of prayer that the church is always taught is about getting control of our. thoughts"],[2221.84,"So if you've heard the Jesus prayer called the prayer of a single thought, that's why."],[2228.08,"Because the average day I have a thousand thoughts running through my head."],[2232.96,"But I try to pray out of a thousand things."],[2235.12,"Yes, exactly. You sit down and try to pray, there's a thousand thoughts."],[2238.08,"And so the Jesus prayer can help us because it's one sentence."],[2242.4,"It's one thought about Christ."],[2245.76,"So repeating it over and over is not repeating a mantra or something."],[2249.62,"Or thinking, well, if I do this a thousand times, I'll have good luck."],[2253.67,"It's about focusing, trying to focus my brain."],[2258.17,"Trying to focus my mind on one thought out of all the others."],[2261.77,"of What it's referred to as the prayer a single thought."],[2266.77,"Yeah. And that's and that's why."],[2269.67,"To try to focus on just one thought."],[2272.79,"Because with me, the devil doesn't need to make me think about evil stuff necessarily."],[2278.75,"I sit down to pray."],[2279.79,"It could be, did you lock the car door?"],[2282.79,"Did you turn the oven off?"],[2284.95,"What was that noise?"],[2286.81,"Like all it doesn't have to be horrible, sinful, wicked stuff."],[2290.99,"It could just be little stuff like that."],[2293.04,"Um, but that's a distracted mind."],[2297.49,"And so when we don't have control of it and we're not thinking about it, a thought comes into our head, and it's sort of like a seed."],[2304.9,"Sort of like all this seed is getting scattered."],[2308.95,"And some of it is going to take root."],[2312.31,"And some of it's going to start to grow into something."],[2316.79,"And when it's done growing, like the weed that it is, it's going to express itself in actions."],[2325.65,"So part of part of repentance or spiritual warfare or life of prayer, all of these things, is learning to get involved with these things at the level of thought before they turn into action."],[2342.53,"Get involved with these things eventually before they even get a chance to take root."],[2348.25,"But often when we're starting, which is still where I am, by the way."],[2352.11,"They've already taken root, you just yank it out the weed."],[2355.31,"Trying to yank it out, get rid of the root too so it doesn't grow back."],[2359.37,"And and move on."],[2362.91,"But this is why, you know, we look at monks on Mount Athos, these incredibly holy people, they've been there their whole lives, and you're like, what could they possibly be talking about in confession?"],[2375.03,"They live on Mount Athos."],[2377.21,"They're doing all that, their whole life is devoted to prayer."],[2379.69,"What could they possibly could be confessing?"],[2381.53,"Well, because they're in tune with that."],[2385.13,"They're in tune with the thought."],[2386.65,"They're they're back at the level of. you know, I let this thought come into my head and I dwelt on it a little bit"],[2394.05,"And I rolled it around a little bit."],[2395.89,"Like, I'm nowhere near that level."],[2397.86,"I'm still at the like, oh man, why did I do that yesterday?"],[2401.78,"Kind of level of right."],[2404.02,"But Working our way back."],[2407.79,"And that comes from this."],[2408.83,"That comes from this commandment."],[2412.0,"Don't let it become adultery."],[2414.16,"Stop it at the point where you're just looking at your neighbor's wife."],[2419.76,"Don't let it become stealing."],[2421.6,"Stop it at the point where you're just admiring somebody's stuff."],[2427.38,"Don't let it become murder or physical violence of any kind."],[2432.14,"Stop it at the point where it's anger or resentment or irritation or whatever it is."],[2437.68,"Those thoughts. Stop it back there."],[2440.17,"That's where we cut it off."],[2442.01,"That's what this commandment is getting at."],[2445.13,"And that's why I think splitting off coveting the house or coveting the wife from the other covets kind of misses the point."],[2453.19,"Obscures what's what's going on here."],[2457.19,"So time-wise and everything."],[2458.71,"I know we're not at the end of a chapter, but we did make it to the end of the nine to ten commandments."],[2464.51,"Uh so we'll go ahead and stop here."],[2467.91,"Thank you, everybody."],[2470.39,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study. of the scriptures on the whole counsel of God"],[2477.79,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2483.07,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.92,"lv":2,"h":"20:7 - Not taking the name in vain: not about expletives","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:7</b>: \"You shall not take the name of the Lord your God <b>in vain</b>; the Lord will not hold him guiltless\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Usual reading is \"usually wrong. Or incomplete. Or a little weak\"</li><li class=\"d1\">growing up: don't say <b>God</b> or related words as an <b>expletive</b>; other expletives okay as not overtly religious</li><li class=\"d1\">substitutes like \"<b>gosh darn it</b>\" - \"better because I changed a couple of letters\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not what this is about\" - \"I'm not afraid to be controversial\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Issue with expletives is <b>not the words</b> - everybody's list of bad words differs by <b>family they grew up in</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>There are no bad words. Only bad intentions.</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">you can <b>destroy someone</b> with words without saying a bad word - doesn't make it better</li><li class=\"d1\">smash your thumb with a hammer: howl or a bad word - \"it hurts\"</li><li class=\"d1\">dirty jokes with substitute words or <b>medical terminology</b> - \"you're not tricking God\"; \"let's be adults\"</li></ul>"},{"t":203.84,"lv":3,"h":"What the commandment is about: carrying his name","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">You don't take the name <b>Yahweh</b> in vain - <b>Pharisees'</b> workaround: never say or write it → \"missing the point\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not saying go yell it or use it in expletives</li><li class=\"d0\">God says over and over he places <b>his name</b> on <b>people and places</b></li><li class=\"d1\">one people: <b>Israel</b> - \"Yahweh, the God of Israel\"</li><li class=\"d0\">People look at <b>how they live, act</b> → reflects on what they think of <b>Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">behave horribly → <b>dishonor to the name of Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Today: anti-Christians cite the <b>behavior of Christians</b> - \"rightly so in some cases\"</li><li class=\"d1\">call yourself Christian → <b>taking the name of Christ</b> and putting it on yourself</li><li class=\"d0\">Funny version: <b>\"honk if you love Jesus\"</b> bumper sticker, you honk, he <b>flips you the bird</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus t-shirts, <b>fish on the car</b>, Orthodox bumper sticker → public identification = <b>responsibility to honor his name</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same dynamic behind <b>honor your father and mother</b> - \"called to something higher\"</li></ul>"},{"t":420.6,"lv":2,"h":"20:8-11 - Remember the Sabbath","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:8-11</b>: six days labor; seventh = <b>Sabbath of the Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no work - you, <b>son, daughter, male and female servant, cattle, stranger</b></li><li class=\"d1\">in six days Lord made heaven and earth; <b>rested</b> the seventh; <b>blessed and hallowed</b> it</li><li class=\"d0\">They're not to do <b>anything</b> on the seventh day</li><li class=\"d0\">Back in Genesis: \"rested\" ≠ took a break - = <b>sitting enthroned</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Modern view: \"day of rest\" because you're <b>worn out</b>; \"God's doing something nice, giving you a day off\" (we want two)</li><li class=\"d1\">remember who it was <b>originally given to</b> - most of history people were <b>farming</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not only Sabbath days → <b>Sabbath years</b></li></ul>"},{"t":486.0,"lv":2,"h":"Sabbath for subsistence farmers: trust","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Crop yield</b> - good or bad harvest, seed, irrigation → for <b>subsistence farmers</b> = will your children survive the winter?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not paying bills and a Netflix subscription\" - will the <b>family live</b>? sell kids into slavery? sell yourself?</li><li class=\"d0\">God: <b>one day in seven</b> you take a break</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I mean you're not doing anything\": not sending <b>slaves, kids, animals, the foreigner</b> out to work</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Seventh year</b>: leave the field, let the <b>poor</b> take what they need; don't harvest</li><li class=\"d0\">This requires <b>great trust</b> - if they do what God said, he'll take care of the crops and yield</li><li class=\"d0\">Teaching them: <b>not they</b> who make the crops grow</li><li class=\"d1\">can't get <b>rain</b> right, good seed, stop <b>blight, locusts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">deceive themselves: \"all based on <b>my hard work</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">breaks force them to trust that <b>God provides</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not just \"God demands trust\" - <b>better for them</b></li></ul>"},{"t":672.5,"lv":3,"h":"Christ to the poor; Sabbath as gift; us","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">What Christ is getting at with <b>dirt poor peasants</b> in Galilee</li><li class=\"d1\">\"don't worry about what you'll <b>eat, drink, wear</b>\" - they think all day about that</li><li class=\"d1\">\"because <b>God is the one taking care of you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They come to trust: it's not my hard work, <b>it's God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I just need to be <b>faithful to God</b>, he takes care of the rest\"</li><li class=\"d1\">don't have to be up all night, toil</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ultimately a gift</b> - if willing to learn</li><li class=\"d0\">Applies to us - a <b>paycheck</b>: \"here's how many hours I work, my hard work\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>who made you healthy enough?</b> who kept you alive to do it?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"my survival is not just up to me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: God can't take a year off? - not asking you to; \"2020, he kind of made us all take a year\"</li></ul>"},{"t":794.9,"lv":2,"h":"20:12 - Honor your father and mother","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:12</b>: \"Honor your father and mother, that it may be well with you and your days long in the land\"</li><li class=\"d0\">We <b>misinterpret</b> - partly because <b>parents want us to</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they want it to mean <b>obey</b>, do whatever they say - \"any port in a storm… the struggle is real\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Like the name commandment: live so as to <b>bring honor</b> to your father and mother</li><li class=\"d1\">modern terms: your <b>family name</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people look at you and say \"wow, you must have come from a <b>great family</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Can't be 100% perfect; can't get there by always doing what we want either</li><li class=\"d0\">But we can live in a way that brings <b>honor, not dishonor or disrespect</b> to our parents, family, <b>heritage</b></li></ul>"},{"t":911.79,"lv":2,"h":"20:13 - You shall not murder","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Define murder\" - other instances of killing; will expand</li><li class=\"d0\">Blunt: <b>Genesis 9</b> after the flood - <b>taking a human life is always wrong, never good</b></li><li class=\"d1\">even if \"justified\" - not even neutral, <b>always bad</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"What about <b>war</b>?\" - talk to someone who killed in war: \"it was not good\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"what they had to do, maybe, in the circumstance\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Self-defense</b> - ask them how they feel; not good</li><li class=\"d0\">Further: someone in a <b>car accident</b> where someone died, not their fault - not \"it's cool\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not real life\" - every human is <b>made in the image of God</b> (Gen 9)</li><li class=\"d1\">any stage of <b>fetal development</b>, any stage of <b>old age</b> → a <b>tragedy</b>, horrible</li><li class=\"d1\">even if \"the <b>best bad option</b> in that moment\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1058.21,"lv":3,"h":"Penance, not punishment: unclean soldiers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Church has always <b>penanced</b> any taking of life - <b>not punished</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a process, longer or shorter by circumstances, to <b>reintegrate</b> into the community</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>healing and restoration</b></li><li class=\"d0\">All the way back in the <b>Torah</b>:</li><li class=\"d1\">God tells Israel to <b>wipe out a giant clan</b> → soldiers <b>unclean</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wash weapons, armor; live <b>outside the camp</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God commanded it because evil had to be stopped - \"<b>still doesn't make killing them good</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"What we call <b>PTSD</b>\" - God knew; church always knew</li><li class=\"d1\">spiritual healing process - \"not a punishment\"</li><li class=\"d1\">telling them \"it's fine, it was justified\" <b>doesn't help</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1173.16,"lv":2,"h":"20:14 - You shall not commit adultery","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Home stretch\"; this one should be clear</li><li class=\"d0\">Old <b>SNL</b> sketch: <b>John Goodman as Moses</b>; <b>Bill Clinton</b> steps out: \"can you be more specific?\" - \"from the 90s\"</li><li class=\"d0\">If you need specific, <b>Christ gets more specific</b>:</li><li class=\"d1\">look at a woman <b>lustfully</b> = adultery</li><li class=\"d1\">not a question of \"what if you just do this?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1233.87,"lv":2,"h":"Commandments directed to men; Thecla","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Point for the commandments on sexual issues: they're all directed <b>toward men</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not that <b>women</b> can't commit sexual sins - they obviously can</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Bronze Age</b>: women didn't get to choose</li><li class=\"d1\">married off at <b>12 or 13</b>; husband takes you whenever; <b>divorces</b> when tired → back to family</li><li class=\"d1\">parents gone → probably <b>prostitute</b>, no other way to make a living</li><li class=\"d0\">No point commanding women where they can't choose → God commands <b>men</b>, \"to <b>protect women</b> from them for the most part, and other men\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Change came from the <b>early church</b>, martyrs like <b>St. Thecla</b></li><li class=\"d1\">women have a right to <b>not marry</b> and devote themselves to God - \"huge\"; Thecla martyred for it</li><li class=\"d1\">once Christians in power → right <b>enshrined</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now women free to choose → commandments apply to them <b>just as much</b></li><li class=\"d1\">woman looks at a man with lust = adultery; \"good thing… also brings <b>responsibility</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1428.47,"lv":2,"h":"20:15 - You shall not steal: private vs personal property","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Different view of property than the ancient world</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Personal property</b> existed: things that are mine that I <b>use</b></li><li class=\"d1\">toothbrush, coffee mug, cell phone, reading glasses</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Private property</b> did <b>not</b> exist: delimit land - \"this is mine, no one else can go there\"</li><li class=\"d1\">or a <b>house I don't live in</b>; they had the house they lived in, used</li><li class=\"d0\">Why it matters - <b>Deuteronomy</b> specific commandments:</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>famine</b>: someone has stockpiled more than needed → take enough to feed your family - <b>not stealing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">take more than you need = stealing; <b>he's stealing by stockpiling</b></li><li class=\"d1\">taking what we'd call private property is <b>not stealing</b>; <b>having</b> it is</li><li class=\"d1\">taking someone's <b>personal property</b> is stealing - punch me and take my phone</li></ul>"},{"t":1527.92,"lv":3,"h":"Stocked fridges, Basil, and the cloak","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">You come into my house, take a <b>sandwich</b> from a stocked fridge with rotting food → \"fine, according to the Torah\"; \"<b>Jean Valjean</b>, totally cool\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Church fathers' quotes make sense only with this principle</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>St. Basil the Great</b>: shoes in your closet <b>belong to the poor</b> and you're stealing them</li><li class=\"d1\">posts it on social media, gets called a \"socialist… commie\"</li><li class=\"d0\">You have shoes you wear; a whole bunch while others have none</li><li class=\"d1\">part of the outrage over the <b>wealth gap</b> - something ingrained</li><li class=\"d0\">Torah: five pairs of shoes fine - unless a neighbor has none → <b>give one pair</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Behind Christ: \"if someone steals this, <b>give them this too</b>\" - the <b>cloak</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no big market for secondhand cloaks - they steal because they're <b>cold</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1746.65,"lv":2,"h":"20:16 - False witness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:16</b>: \"You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Means \"don't lie\"? Wrong - \"<b>Immanuel Kant</b> has entered the chat\", that's where the idea comes from</li><li class=\"d0\">Very literal: <b>testifying</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no courts - at the <b>city gates</b>; need <b>two witnesses</b> making the same accusation, then trial</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>false accusations</b>, condemning others falsely</li><li class=\"d0\">More against <b>gossip</b> than lying</li><li class=\"d1\">lying under oath applies; but <b>gossip, slander, ruining reputation</b> violate it</li></ul>"},{"t":1826.0,"lv":3,"h":"Kant and the Nazis at the door","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Kant</b>: lying favorite example - \"what if everyone lied? world falls apart\" → always tell the truth</li><li class=\"d0\">Nazi soldiers at the door: \"hiding any Jews?\" - must say yes? \"Of course you don't\" - \"ridiculous\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I try to talk about the Khmer Rouge\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Genesis examples: <b>Judah and Tamar</b>, <b>Jacob</b> - deception</li><li class=\"d1\">trickery vs not telling: <b>divert attention</b>, don't change the truth</li><li class=\"d1\">you don't tell a <b>three-year-old</b> everyone will die someday - not lying</li></ul>"},{"t":1929.2,"lv":3,"h":"Deception for justice; saving a life","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Genesis: <b>deception to bring about justice</b> isn't sin - often all you have</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Tamar</b>: widow twice over, sent back to family, no power, no court case → only deception</li><li class=\"d1\">Nazis have far more power than Dutch families hiding Jews → <b>save an innocent life</b> by deception</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not what this commandment is about\" - and <b>Jewish interpretation</b>:</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>saving a human life never violates a commandment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">break the <b>Sabbath</b>, lie, bear false witness in court - \"adultery… don't know how that saves a life\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Kant's categorical imperative - \"18th century Germans, man\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Again: <b>destroying another's reputation</b> - gossip, slander, false accusation</li><li class=\"d1\">epidemic: whole magazines and TV channels, \"people delighting in it\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2063.29,"lv":2,"h":"20:17 - You shall not covet","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Final one or two commandments, depending on the split</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Neither shall you covet his field… male servant… ox, donkey… <b>whatever belongs to your neighbor</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Heard: when Christ discusses commandments he <b>ratchets it up</b></li><li class=\"d1\">adultery → lust in your heart; murder → \"<b>you fool</b>\", hate = killed</li><li class=\"d0\">\"This is why that's wrong\":</li><li class=\"d1\">coveting neighbor's wife = <b>thinking about adultery</b>; neighbor's property = <b>thinking about stealing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">This one = the <b>thinking, planning, fantasizing, dwelling</b> that precedes the others</li><li class=\"d1\">wanting, desiring; \"I need it\"; \"this is the right thing to do\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>lead-in to all the others</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2178.0,"lv":2,"h":"Every sin starts as a thought: the Jesus Prayer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Every sinful action starts as a thought</b>; a thousand a day, \"no real control\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Discipline of prayer = getting control of our <b>thoughts</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jesus Prayer</b> = \"<b>prayer of a single thought</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sit down to pray → a thousand thoughts: \"did you lock the car? turn off the oven? what was that noise?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">one sentence, one thought about Christ - <b>not a mantra</b>, not \"a thousand times and good luck\"</li><li class=\"d1\">focus the mind on one thought</li><li class=\"d0\">The devil needn't make me think evil - <b>distracted mind</b> is enough</li></ul>"},{"t":2297.49,"lv":3,"h":"Seeds, Athos, and stopping it early","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Thought = <b>seed</b> scattered; some <b>takes root</b>, grows into a <b>weed</b> → expressed in actions</li><li class=\"d0\">Repentance, spiritual warfare, prayer → deal at the <b>level of thought</b> before action</li><li class=\"d1\">before it takes root; often \"still where I am\" - already rooted: yank it out <b>with the root</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Monks on Mount Athos</b> - what could they confess?</li><li class=\"d1\">in tune with the thought: \"I let it in, <b>dwelt</b>, rolled it around\"; \"I'm nowhere near that level\"</li><li class=\"d0\">From this commandment: <b>stop it early</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not adultery → stop at <b>looking at your neighbor's wife</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not stealing → stop at <b>admiring stuff</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not murder/violence → stop at <b>anger, resentment, irritation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Splitting off coveting house/wife from the rest \"<b>obscures what's going on</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Made it to the end of the nine/ten commandments - stop here; not end of chapter</li></ul>"}]});
